<header><p class="st-kicker">sultanate · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Sultanate of Touggourt</h1><p class="st-meta">1414 CE – 1854 CE (approx.) · capital Touggourt</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An oasis sultanate of the Oued Righ in the Algerian Sahara, ruled by the Banu Djellab dynasty for over four centuries until the French conquest.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banu-djellab">Banu Djellab</a>, traditionally said to be of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marinid-dynasty">Marinid</a> descent, established themselves as rulers of Touggourt and the oases of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oued-righ">Oued Righ valley</a> around 1414. Their town lay on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caravan-trade">caravan routes</a> linking the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> coast with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahara">Sahara</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The sultans governed a chain of palm oases producing dates, depending on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/well">wells</a> and irrigation. The population mixed Arabic-speaking and Berber-speaking groups, as well as people of sub-Saharan origin. Touggourt rivalled the nearby <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sultanate-of-ouargla">Sultanate of Ouargla</a> and was at times tributary to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/regency-of-algiers">Regency of Algiers</a>, whose beys of Constantine sent expeditions to collect tribute.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Dynastic quarrels weakened the state in the 19th century. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/french-algeria">French Algeria</a> occupied Touggourt in 1854 and installed a pliant ruler, ending <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banu-djellab">Djellab</a> independence; the town became a military post in the French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahara">Sahara</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/sultanate-of-touggourt.jpg" alt="Sultanate of Touggourt" width="320" height="260"><figcaption>Image: Sambott27 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ben_Djellab_Palace,_Touggourt.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1414 CE – 1854 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>sultanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Touggourt</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic, Berber</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/algeria">Algeria</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Banu Djellab, Touggourt</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1634&amp;focus=sultanate-of-touggourt" aria-label="Sultanate of Touggourt on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4835 976 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Sultanate of Touggourt lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5155 1232L5077 1108M5155 1232L5077 1108"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5077 1108h0M5077 1108h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5155 1232h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5155 1232h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Touggourt. <a href="/atlas?year=1634&amp;focus=sultanate-of-touggourt">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

